    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, so if we're basically admitting there's a \"moral imperative\" to fix these wrongs, does that mean the argument for keepin' things in universal museums is actually just an excuse to keep holding onto stolen goods? like, can you even make a strong academic case for it anymore that isn't just \"we're better at guarding it\" or something? i want to make sure we aren't giving too much weight to a side that's basically outdated.",
